een), yet the only proving criterion for cross-pass survival is a unit test asserting the file is staged by `_commit_binding_store_snapshot` and in its idempotency set — no check that the committed record is actually re-read and honored on the NEXT pass's fresh checkout.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5f92b27ff36897a6","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 ('The file must be COMMITTED to the tickets branch') and AC 'impossible_links.json is staged by _commit_binding_store_snapshot'","norm_id":"nb5620a6290dcd025","priority":0.2063,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["Staging is wired correctly in the unit test but the committed file is not read on the next pass's checkout (wrong path, not pulled, read after the skip decision), so convergence still fails in production while every listed test is green"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add: 'Given a committed impossible_links.json, a fresh reconciler run (simulating a new CI checkout) loads the record from the committed file and skips the matching link write, counting zero rebar.link invocations for that triple.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether impossible_links.py's atomic write reuses rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write (or the binding_store/alert_store idiom) rather than hand-rolling a fourth temp+os.replace copy.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:57 'Atomically write ``data`` to ``path`` (temp-in-same-dir + os.replace)'","binding_store.py:307, alert_store.py:100, pass_io.py:156, get_rotation.py:105 all already implement temp+os.replace","alert_store.py:87 uses tempfile + fsync + os.replace — a hand-rolled copy in the new module could omit the fsync and diverge"],"finding":"The plan describes the store's durability as 'Written by temp-file + atomic os.replace' as though implementing the atomic-write mechanism afresh, but the codebase already provides rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write and sibling reconciler state files (binding_store.py, alert_store.py, pass_io.py, get_rotation.py) all use the identical temp-in-same-dir + os.replace idiom (some with fsync). Reusing the existing helper avoids a fourth hand-rolled copy that could silently diverge (e.g. omit fsync).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faaff000224fb5a0e","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 (Fail-open and hygiene): 'Written by temp-file + atomic os.replace, only when something changed'","norm_id":"n802e3cadb180d2d7","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A new impossible_links.py that reimplements os.replace without fsync degrades crash-durability relative to alert_store.py."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Have the store persist via rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write (or delegate to the same helper binding_store/alert_store use), rather than restating the temp-file + os.replace mechanism inline.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confir